  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Make the ENTIRE getting-started vertical work END-TO-END through the HTTP wire and prove it with a
    WebApplicationFactory test: a user opens the Compose workspace, chooses "Browse / open file" or "Upload"
    (transient mount) or "Search for Document" (load), the document renders in the editor, and on first Save
    the transient draft is PERSISTED as a real `sprk_document` in the user's Business-Unit SPE container
    (create-on-save). Today this is non-functional over HTTP despite tasks 013/014/015 being marked ✅ —
    the create-on-save service backbone (ComposeService.SaveAsync transient branch) is correct but is DEAD
    CODE over HTTP because the client never resolves/sends the containerId, the Save route/DTO/guards/button
    all block the transient path, and no test drives the slice through the wire. Close register Cluster 1
    gaps 1.1–1.8 and land the anti-recurrence test. Loads (search, open-in-Compose) and replace-save already
    work — verify, do not rebuild them.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Full-stack developer fluent in the Compose entry-path mounts (ComposeWorkspace reducer, transient/loaded
    state), the BFF create-on-save path (ComposeService.SaveAsync + SpeFileStore facade), the 7 Create*Wizard
    BU→container convention (EntityCreationService / Xrm.WebApi), and WebApplicationFactory integration tests.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Browse/Upload → transient mount → Save persists a byte-correct `.docx` as a new `sprk_document` in the
    resolved BU container and rebinds the session; Search/open-in-Compose → load still works. Every hop
    connects over HTTP. A WebApplicationFactory test drives upload→save→persist through POST endpoints and
    asserts the sprk_document + SPE item exist. All 8 Cluster-1 gaps closed; DEF-06/DEF-07 removed from the
    defer list (fixed, not deferred).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Source of truth: notes/e2e-gap-register.md Cluster 1 (gaps 1.1–1.8) with exact file:line evidence, and
      design.md §2.7 (create-on-save = upgrade of PromoteIfEphemeralAsync to full ingestion parity). Owner
      decisions in force: (Path 1, approved 2026-07-09) resolve BU→container CLIENT-SIDE via the existing
      EntityCreationService / Xrm.WebApi convention — do NOT add a BFF BU→container resolver (Fork A). Fork-C
      profile-analysis stays deferred to core (non-terminal deferred signal; aggregate=Partial) — do NOT build it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="client-workspace" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx — triggerSave (send containerId; gate on containerId||isDirty||transient not effectiveDriveId — gaps 1.4/1.2); saveSucceeded must write documentSpeId into documentRef.speDriveItemId (gap 1.7).</file>
      <file purpose="client-reducer" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.types.ts — mountTransient must carry containerId; saveSucceeded reducer must update speDriveItemId (gaps 1.3/1.7).</file>
      <file purpose="client-toolbar" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeToolbar.tsx — Save button: gate on isDirty||hasTransientDraft; compute hasDocument as "loaded" not "has id" (gap 1.5 / DEF-07 + the second hasDocument lock).</file>
      <file purpose="client-editor" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx — the docxBytes effect must NOT force onDirtyChange(false) for a TRANSIENT mount (gap 1.6 / DEF-01).</file>
      <file purpose="host-bu-resolve" edit="true">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/App.tsx (+ the compose mount host) — resolve the user's BU containerId via EntityCreationService/Xrm.WebApi and thread it in (STOP setting containerId: undefined) (gap 1.3).</file>
      <file purpose="bu-resolver-REUSE" edit="false">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts — the resolveBusinessUnitContainerId (businessunit.sprk_containerid) reuse target; the 7 Create*Wizard services use it. Do NOT reimplement.</file>
      <file purpose="server-endpoint" edit="true">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs — add containerId to SaveComposeDocumentBody; add a transient-create route (or make documentSpeId/driveId optional) so a draft with no SPE item can be saved; map ContainerId + null DocumentSpeId into SaveComposeDocumentRequest (gaps 1.1/1.2); add annotations/rehydrate fields is OUT of scope (that is task 103).</file>
      <file purpose="server-service-REUSE" edit="false">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — SaveAsync transient branch (container→record→indexing) is already correct; do NOT rewrite it — just make it REACHABLE. IComposeService.cs DTO already carries ContainerId.</file>
      <file purpose="association" edit="true">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/compose/useCreateOnSaveAssociation.ts — call associate(newDocumentId) from the save-completion flow (gap 1.8); currently only invoked in a test.</file>
      <file purpose="e2e-test" edit="true">tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/ComposeCreateOnSaveEndpointContractTests.cs (NEW) — the anti-recurrence WebApplicationFactory slice test.</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner-Path1">BU→container resolved CLIENT-SIDE via EntityCreationService / Xrm.WebApi (the 7-wizard convention). NO new BFF BU→container resolver.</constraint>
    <constraint source="cleanGuid">Every GUID that enters an @odata.bind or /entityset(guid) URL from an Xrm source (BU resolution businessunit id, the createRecord-returned sprk_document id, the parent-association @odata.bind) MUST be wrapped with `cleanGuid` from `@spaarke/ui-components` (no-op on bare GUIDs; deep-import fallback for stale tarballs). Do NOT hand-roll `.replace(/[{}]/g,'')`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">SPE writes go through the SpeFileStore/Infrastructure facade; no Microsoft.Graph types leak into Services/Compose.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-005">Persist to the SPE container resolved from the user's BU.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Services/Compose injects no AI internals; Fork-C profile analysis stays a deferred signal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Client save/resolve fetches use @spaarke/auth (and Xrm.WebApi for host Dataverse).</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-defer">Fix all 8 gaps in this pass; remove DEF-06/DEF-07 from notes/defer-issues.md (fixed, not deferred). Do NOT file new deferrals for in-scope gaps.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-hygiene">BFF-touching: report publish-size delta vs 49.63 MB baseline + CVE scan.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>compose/create-on-save, spe-persistence, bu-container-resolution, webapplicationfactory-e2e</topic>
