  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load the register Cluster 1 + this POML. Read the 8 broken hops at their cited file:line and the EntityCreationService BU→container reuse target. Confirm the ComposeService.SaveAsync transient branch is present and correct (it is — do not rewrite).</step>
    <step order="1">Server: add `containerId` to SaveComposeDocumentBody; add a transient-create route (or relax the id/driveId requirement) so a draft with no SPE item reaches the transient branch; map ContainerId + null DocumentSpeId into the request (gaps 1.1/1.2).</step>
    <step order="2">Client BU resolution: resolve the user's BU containerId via EntityCreationService/Xrm.WebApi at the host; thread it prop → mountTransient → state.documentRef.containerId (gap 1.3). Wrap any Xrm GUID going into OData with cleanGuid.</step>
    <step order="3">Client save: send containerId in the triggerSave body; gate triggerSave + the Save button on containerId||isDirty||transientDraft (gaps 1.4/1.5); stop the transient-mount dirty-reset (gap 1.6); on saveSucceeded write the returned documentSpeId into documentRef.speDriveItemId (gap 1.7).</step>
    <step order="4">Association: call useCreateOnSaveAssociation.associate(newDocumentId) from the save-completion flow (gap 1.8), cleanGuid on the @odata.bind. (Hosting the prompt in the Tier-2c dialog may stay minimal — the REQUIRED bar is that a chosen parent persists at save.)</step>
    <step order="5">ANTI-RECURRENCE TEST (definition-of-done, non-waivable): add ComposeCreateOnSaveEndpointContractTests — a WebApplicationFactory test that POSTs an upload then the save (with containerId, no documentSpeId) through the real endpoints and asserts a new sprk_document + SPE item exist and the session rebinds. This is the pattern every later remediation task reuses.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify: dotnet build + dotnet test (new + Compose regression); Compose.Components tsc + jest; publish-size + CVE. Run Step 9.5 (code-review + adr-check) UNCONDITIONALLY. Update the 100 POML notes; remove DEF-06/DEF-07 from defer-issues.md. Do NOT edit TASK-INDEX/current-task (main session reconciles).</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">ComposeEndpoints.cs (containerId wire DTO + transient-create route)</output>
    <output type="code">ComposeWorkspace.tsx + .types.ts + ComposeToolbar.tsx + ComposeEditor.tsx (containerId thread, save gates, dirty-reset fix, speId carry-back)</output>
    <output type="code">App.tsx / compose mount host (BU containerId resolution via EntityCreationService, cleanGuid)</output>
    <output type="code">useCreateOnSaveAssociation wired into save-completion</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/ComposeCreateOnSaveEndpointContractTests.cs (WebApplicationFactory upload→save→persist slice)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Browse/open-file → transient mount → Save persists a new sprk_document in the resolved BU container; SaveComposeDocumentBody carries containerId and the client sends it (gaps 1.1–1.4 closed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Upload → transient mount → Save persists byte-correct .docx (FR-06a: original-if-unedited branch still honored) as a new sprk_document.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Save button is enabled for a transient mount (gated on isDirty||hasTransientDraft, not documentId); the transient dirty-reset no longer fires (gaps 1.5/1.6).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On save success the client writes the server-minted documentSpeId into documentRef.speDriveItemId so a second Save targets the real item (gap 1.7).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A chosen parent association persists at save via associate(newDocumentId) (gap 1.8); every Xrm GUID entering an OData bind is wrapped with cleanGuid.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Search-for-Document and open-in-Compose LOAD paths still work (verified, not rebuilt).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A WebApplicationFactory test drives upload→save→persist through the real POST endpoints and asserts the sprk_document + SPE item exist (anti-recurrence definition-of-done).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DEF-06 and DEF-07 removed from notes/defer-issues.md (fixed). No new deferrals filed for in-scope gaps. BFF publish-size delta + CVE reported; Step 9.5 clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
